---
description: Read _brain memory before work; capture non-derivable learnings at close
alwaysApply: true
---

# Memory — `_brain`

Durable, non-derivable knowledge lives in `_brain/` (committed, agent-agnostic).

- Before non-trivial work, read `@_brain/INDEX.md` and open the detail files whose
  one-line hook matches the task.
- A record reflects what was true when written — verify any file/flag/command/path it
  names still exists before acting on it.
- At phase/PRD close, if you hit something not derivable from the code, add
  `_brain/learnings/<slug>.md` (see `_brain/_templates/learning.md`) and its `INDEX.md`
  pointer. Never store what the repo already records.
